{"h": {"measure": "A", "k": 100, "noise": "L"}, "sp": "nb", "rep": 138, "hyps": [{"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "skip_connect", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "higher", "why": "Adding a residual path where none exists gives far larger gains than replacing an existing conv/pool on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Replacing the crucial direct skip with a conv removes the residual path and hurts, whereas filling an empty edge 3 helps a lot."}, {"edit_edge": 3, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "skip_connect", "direction": "lower", "why": "Deleting the input-output skip is much more damaging than deleting a conv on edge 3."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Without the direct 0->3 path, edge 5 is a key route to the output, so removing it is catastrophic."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "none", "cond_edge": 3, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "When edge 3 is absent, node 1 carries the main signal, so cutting edge 0 severely disconnects the cell."}, {"edit_edge": 2, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 2, "cond_op": "nor_conv_1x1", "direction": "lower", "why": "Swapping a 1x1 conv for a 3x3 conv adds little capacity compared with replacing a pool, skip, or empty edge."}, {"edit_edge": 1, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 1, "cond_op": "none", "direction": "lower", "why": "Filling an empty edge 1 yields smaller gains than upgrading an existing skip/pool/1x1 op on edge 1."}, {"edit_edge": 5, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 5, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing a parameter-free pool with a conv on the final edge helps, while adding a conv to an empty edge 5 tends to hurt."}, {"edit_edge": 0, "edit_op": "nor_conv_3x3", "cond_edge": 0, "cond_op": "avg_pool_3x3", "direction": "higher", "why": "Replacing an avg pool with a conv o